Counterfactual for koniz-dev/flutter-starter#168
================================================

What was run
------------
The new tests from this change, executed against the *pre-fix* library code.
Both production files were reverted to origin/main (a55674d) while the three
test files kept their new content:

    git checkout origin/main -- \
      lib/features/auth/data/repositories/auth_repository_impl.dart \
      lib/features/auth/data/datasources/auth_local_datasource.dart

    flutter test \
      test/features/auth/data/repositories/auth_repository_impl_test.dart \
      test/features/auth/data/datasources/auth_local_datasource_test.dart \
      test/core/network/forced_logout_cache_test.dart --timeout=5m

Result: exit 1, "00:00 +70 -10: Some tests failed."

10 of the 12 new assertions fail without the fix. The two that pass without it
are the mirror-case guards ("an HTTP cache throwing ... is still reported after
a clean local teardown"), which exercise a chain whose first step succeeds and
so were never affected by the coupling - they exist to stop the fix from
swallowing a last-step failure into a Success, not to demonstrate the defect.

The failures are the defect itself, in four shapes:

  * `httpCache.clearCalls` is 0 where 1 is required - the explicit logout
    skipped the HTTP response cache entirely because the local teardown threw.
  * both tokens still readable after `clearCache()` - `clearAllTokens()` never
    ran because the user-blob removal threw.
  * a bare `StateError` escaping `clearCache()` instead of the declared
    `CacheException` - the `on Exception` half of the defect.
  * the #114 equivalence assertion reporting the two paths' device states as
    unequal.

